SSL/TLS

People still commonly say "SSL certificate", but technically modern certificates are used with TLS.

Interview answer

SSL was the older security protocol. TLS is its successor and is the protocol used today. When people say SSL/TLS, they usually mean TLS.

For example:

HTTPS
  ↓
HTTP + TLS
  ↓
Secure encrypted communication

So when you hear "SSL termination", in modern systems it usually means TLS termination.
